// case: shadowed-system-member
// what: a local named `system` was matched to the system builtin by its
//      spelling, so `system.trim()` was diagnosed as a member of the builtin
//      and not of the string the local holds. The receiver is its type: the
//      local shadows the builtin, so the string member set answers, and `trim`
//      is refused by the string rule. The message names the type it read.
// expect-error: 'string' has no member 'trim'.
fn main() -> int {
    val system = "  padded  "
    print(system.trim())
    return 0
}
